Gases and Applications — Linde (@gas-gases-handbook: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gas-sources) { r_72580QNZ60FMQAARB8ZG7SRTFT
Linde. *Gases and Applications*, introduction to the 2017 edition, with copyright 2020 in the inspected copy. [Complete publisher-hosted 261-page handbook](https://static.prd.echannel.linde.com/wcsstore/REN_Industrial_Gas_Store/HiQ_Gas_and_applications_handbook_2017_EN.pdf).

Read the introduction and guide to specification tables first. Work through the full gas and mixture families over the production and delivery sections, comparing the stated application, impurity panel, phase and equipment context. Use individual entries as dated examples, not current purchasing specifications.

The title, edition/copyright notices, contents and specification explanations were inspected on 30 October 2026. The guide distinguishes a purity code from explicit impurity limits and identifies the phase basis for liquefied-gas data. A displayed purity percentage cannot stand in for an application's complete acceptance criteria.

Copyright Linde, all rights reserved; authorized public reading does not grant copying or adaptation of its tables and figures. Keep the handbook external. Manufacturer examples need independent physical and metrological scrutiny alongside the scholarly sources.

